  "prompt": "[system]\n\n    You generate compact, robust Python TSP metaheuristics.\n    You must follow the requested interface exactly, always preserve tour validity.\n    \n\n[user]\nPARENTS:\nCandidate cand_000007: best_improve_2opt\n\nStatus: valid; distance: 17.4019\n\nThought: Start from nearest neighbor tour, then repeatedly apply the best 2-opt edge exchange (the one yielding maximum cost reduction) until no improving move exists. This intensifies search by making the most progress in each iteration.\n\nCode:\n\n```python\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix):\n    n = distance_matrix.shape[0]\n    # nearest neighbor construction\n    tour = [0]\n    unvisited = set(range(1, n))\n    curr = 0\n    while unvisited:\n        nxt = min(unvisited, key=lambda c: distance_matrix[curr, c])\n        tour.append(nxt)\n        unvisited.remove(nxt)\n        curr = nxt\n    tour = np.array(tour, dtype=np.int32)\n    \n    def tour_cost(t):\n        cost = 0.0\n        for k in range(n):\n            cost += distance_matrix[t[k], t[(k+1)%n]]\n        return cost\n    \n    best_cost = tour_cost(tour)\n    report_best_tour(tour.copy())\n    improved = True\n    while improved:\n        improved = False\n        best_delta = 0.0\n        best_i = best_j = -1\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i+2, n):\n                a, b = tour[i], tour[(i+1)%n]\n                c, d = tour[j], tour[(j+1)%n]\n                delta = distance_matrix[a,c] + distance_matrix[b,d] - (distance_matrix[a,b] + distance_matrix[c,d])\n                if delta < best_delta:\n                    best_delta = delta\n                    best_i, best_j = i, j\n        if best_delta < 0:\n            i, j = best_i, best_j\n            tour[i+1:j+1] = tour[i+1:j+1][::-1]\n            cost = tour_cost(tour)\n            if cost < best_cost:\n                best_cost = cost\n                report_best_tour(tour.copy())\n            improved = True\n    return tour\n\n```\n\nVERBAL GRADIENT: follow the reflection below as the primary source of change.\n\nUse the supplied parents as supporting evidence only.\n\nPARENT-SPECIFIC LLM REFLECTIONS:\n\nParent cand_000007 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Best-improving 2-opt on nearest neighbor tour achieved 17.40 mean distance, improving over parent by 1% without timeouts.\n- Aim: Reduce mean tour length by escaping local optima via diversification or perturbation.\n- Preserve: nearest neighbor construction; steepest descent 2-opt; best-tour reporting\n- Change: Add a ruin-and-recreate restart after local optimum; Apply a random double-bridge move when no improvement found\n- Avoid: Compromising valid permutation guarantee; Exceeding timeout budget; Removing report_best_tour calls\n\nParent cand_000004 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Nearest neighbor plus single-move 2-opt yields valid tours with moderate quality and no timeouts, but local search is limited.\n- Aim: Improve tour quality by enabling full 2-opt scanning and adding restarts with random perturbation.\n- Preserve: nearest neighbor construction; valid permutation guarantee; timeout robustness\n- Change: replace single-move 2-opt with full-scan 2-opt until local minimum; add outer restart loop with randomized initial tours or perturbation\n- Avoid: breaking valid permutation; exceeding timeout; introducing runtime errors\n\nParent cand_000010 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Candidate retained same tour length as parent (18.016) with 100% valid tours, but mean runtime increased from 9.21s to 10.46s.\n- Aim: Reduce tour length by enhancing local search or adding diversification without causing timeout.\n- Preserve: farthest insertion construction; 2-opt improvement; report_best_tour calls; valid permutation guarantee\n- Change: exhaustive 2-opt without early break; add double-bridge kick for diversification\n- Avoid: exceeding timeout; breaking permutation validity; degrading construction quality\n\nDistance is the search objective for T